{"title":"Ostrowski's criterion","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Ostrowski's Criterion states that:\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b4791a0f6666d8d8c4abdeedd4ffcb79680b75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=a_nx^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\\cdots+a_1x+a_0\\in \\mathbb{Z}[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"377\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a prime and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/487117ed0a9d60848f80e992e01223ec80ee6319.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_0|&gt;|a_n|+|a_{n-1}|+\\cdots+|a_1|\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" />\nthen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is irreducible.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ostrowski%27s_criterion&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/6/9f6582a3fa230126b94691670deb7373d7b88440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16cddaa2ff95af4b6f4869ca9c2888429c69c665.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|a_0|=|a_1\\phi+\\cdots+a_n\\phi^n|\\leq |a_1|+\\cdots+|a_n|\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"18\" />\na contradiction. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5ab2753d78334ab7b7041a5e5ce3337205076e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea1fb901c032525b58ac56d17256a25d2ba56f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=g(x)h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/051410937878e0fc000ef1293e589e80ee759a4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)=a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/761b9da027f3bd1633e8d6f915fb79a26e6b8c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73cf44c99fcdc573af387bc056c295eb14ecaa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is 1. WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f42ff6e02f0df88b17dbab5135423850dce5e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(0)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the leading coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781adf6c112c087237297f5621d03e229174d440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1,\\phi_2,\\cdots,\\phi_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b6fa28ad4d01b0f8f82d251f43401714e0fdd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1&lt;|\\phi_1\\phi_2\\cdots \\phi_n|=\\frac{1}{|b|}\\leq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"205\" height=\"41\" />. This is a contradiction, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is irreducible.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Ostrowski%27s_criterion&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018102412\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.015 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 77/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 312/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3683/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.383      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.383      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16651:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018102412 and revision id 240889. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}